cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RoT MoE - a nine-lens Mixture-of-Experts router for Claude Code, specified in Lean 4"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Saimonokuma"
    website: "https://github.com/Nova-Violet-Role"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nova-Violet-Role/RoT-MoE"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - EUPL-1.2
version: 0.7.2
date-released: 2026-08-04
abstract: >-
  A Mixture-of-Experts router for Claude Code: nine lenses, a measured R/s+
  divergence gauge, and TIER 1 keyword routing, shipped in two independent
  implementations (POSIX shell and PowerShell) that are cross-diffed
  byte-for-byte. The specification is 281 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems with
  zero sorry and zero native_decide, re-verified by the Lean kernel via
  leanchecker. An executable checker binds the proofs to the shipped hooks and
  is itself mutation-tested; the packet is additionally verified by a live
  Claude Code session in which the router is observed firing, with the
  uninstalled run recorded as the negative control.
